{"id": "mmlupro-12171", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "Consider an example of forced convection within a pipe. The local heat transfer coefficient is valid at the point it is evaluated at, and in its immediate vicinity. When the length of pipe as a whole is of concern, the average heat transfer coefficient applies. The average temperature difference is defined as (T_s - T)_av= [{(T_s - T_in) + (T_s - T_out)} / 2] where T_s = wall surface temperature T_in = bulk fluid temperature at entrance T_out = bulk fluid temperature at exit. Derive the average heat transfer coefficienth_avin terms of the local coefficienth_x.", "options": ["h_av= [{^L\\int_0h_x(T_s + T)dx} / (T_s -T_av)]", "h_av= [{^L\\int_0(h_x + T)dx} / (T_s - T_av)]", "h_av= [{^L\\int_0h_x(T_s - T)dx} / {(T_s - T_in) + (T_s - T_out)}]", "h_av= [{^L\\int_0h_x(T_s - T)^2dx} / (T_s - T_av)]", "h_av= [{^L\\int_0h_x(T_s - T)dx} / (T_in - T_out)]", "h_av= [{^L\\int_0h_x(T_s - T)dx} / L]", "h_av= [{^L\\int_0h_x(T_s - T)dx} / (T_s -T_av)]", "h_av= [{^L\\int_0h_xdx} / (T_s - T_av)]", "h_av= [{^L\\int_0h_x(T_s - T)dx} / (T_s + T_av)]", "h_av= [{^L\\int_0h_x(T_s - T)dx} / 2\\piR^ L]", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 6, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "engineering", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "calib"}
{"id": "mmlupro-8502", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "Suppose ${X_n:n\\geq 1}$ be independent and exponentially distributed with parameter 1. what is the probability $P(\\limsup _{n \\rightarrow infty} X_n/\\log(n)=1)? Return a numeric value.", "options": ["0.69314718056 (1/ln(2))", "1.0", "0.36787944117 (1/e)", "0.0", "0.1", "0.2", "0.5", "0.63212055882 (1 - 1/e)", "0.845350936 (1 - 1/\u03c0)", "0.9", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 1, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "math", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
{"id": "mmlupro-1776", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "While visiting at his son's home, a grandfather tripped on a toy left on the floor by his four-year- old grandson. The grandfather fell and was severely injured. The grandfather regularly visited his son's home and was aware that the grandson routinely left toys scattered about the house. The son had never warned the grandfather to look out for toys. The grandfather brought an action against his son to recover for his injuries. At trial, after the close of evidence, both the grandfather and the son have moved for judgment as a matter of law as to liability. The jurisdiction has abolished intra-family immunity and applies the traditional rules of landowner liability. What action should the court take?", "options": ["Deny both motions and submit the case to the jury based on negligence.", "Grant the grandfather's motion, because the son had a duty to maintain a safe environment for visitors.", "Deny the grandfather's motion, because the son had no duty to control the behavior of his child.", "Grant both motions, as both parties share equal liability for the incident.", "Deny both motions and submit the case to the jury based on strict liability.", "Grant the son's motion, because the grandfather failed to exercise due care in avoiding the toy.", "Grant the son's motion, because the son had no duty to warn that the grandson might leave toys on the floor.", "Grant the son's motion, because the grandfather was aware of the risk and still chose to visit.", "Deny both motions and submit the case to the jury based on premises liability.", "Grant the grandfather's motion, because the son is liable as a matter of law for failing to warn about the risk of toys being left on the floor.", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 6, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "law", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
{"id": "mmlupro-9517", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "For a uniform sphere with moments of inertia I_1 = I_2 = I_3, use the Euler equations to find the equation of motion of the sphere.", "options": ["\\dot{\\omega} = 0", "\\omega = 0", "\\omega = I\\dot{\\omega}", "\\omega \\propto t", "N = const", "\\omega = const", "\\dot{N} = const", "I = const", "N = I\\omega", "\\omega = I/N", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 5, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "physics", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
