{"id": "mmlupro-2951", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "In Japan, the frequency of the R-governed multiple drug-resistant strain ofShigella, which causes dysentery, rose from 0.2 percent in 1953 to 58 percent in 1965. Also, 84 percent of the E. coli and 90 percent of Proteus collected from affected hospital patients showed similar resistance. How could such an increase happen?", "options": ["The bacteria mutated rapidly", "The bacteria developed immunity to antibiotics", "Increased use of antibacterial soaps and disinfectants in hospitals", "Transfer of resistance genes from non-pathogenic to pathogenic bacteria through horizontal gene transfer", "Natural selection favored bacteria that were inherently resistant to antibiotics", "Over-prescription of antibiotics in livestock agriculture leading to cross-species transfer of resistance", "Indiscriminate use of antibiotics selected for drug-resistant bacteria which can then pass their resistance to potentially harmful strains.", "A decline in vaccination rates leading to increased bacterial spread", "Introduction of new antibiotics that were less effective against resistant strains", "The bacteria were genetically modified", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 6, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "biology", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
{"id": "mmlupro-3368", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "How does asexual reproduction take place in the bryophytes ?In the lower vascular plants?", "options": ["Bryophytes reproduce asexually by producing seeds", "Both bryophytes and lower vascular plants reproduce asexually by producing tubers", "Lower vascular plants do not carry out asexual reproduction", "Lower vascular plants reproduce asexually only through fragmentation", "Lower vascular plants use spore formation while bryophytes use binary fission", "Bryophytes and lower vascular plants reproduce asexually only through spore dispersal by wind", "Bryophytes and some lower vascular plants carry out asexual reproduction by budding, forming gemmae cups, vegetative reproduction, or formation of deciduous leaf-borne buds.", "Both bryophytes and lower vascular plants reproduce asexually exclusively by vegetative reproduction", "Bryophytes reproduce only sexually", "Bryophytes reproduce by spore formation", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 6, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "biology", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
