{"id": "mmlupro-3759", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "A chemist has one mole of X atoms. He finds that when half of the X atoms transfer one electron to the other half, 409 kJ must be added. If all of the resulting X^- ions are subsequently converted to X+ ions, an additional 733 kJ must be added. Find the ionization potential, and the electron affinity of X.", "options": ["Ionization potential: 13.84eV/atom, Electron affinity: 0.36eV/atom", "Ionization potential: 14.84eV/atom, Electron affinity: 1.36eV/atom", "Ionization potential: 11.84eV/atom, Electron affinity: 5.36eV/atom", "Ionization potential: 11.84eV/atom, Electron affinity: 3.36eV/atom", "Ionization potential: 10.84eV/atom, Electron affinity: 4.36eV/atom", "Ionization potential: 9.84eV/atom, Electron affinity: 6.36eV/atom", "Ionization potential: 8.84eV/atom, Electron affinity: 7.36eV/atom", "Ionization potential: 12.84eV/atom, Electron affinity: 2.36eV/atom", "Ionization potential: 12.84eV/atom, Electron affinity: 4.36eV/atom", "Ionization potential: 10.84eV/atom, Electron affinity: 3.36eV/atom", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 3, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "chemistry", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
{"id": "mmlupro-7395", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "TheRicardiantheory of land rents led to a movement in the late nineteenth century called the single-tax movement. What was the goal of this movement and what was its economic rationale?", "options": ["To tax only corporate profits as a means of funding government", "To eliminate all taxes", "To eliminate all taxes but a tax on land", "To increase all taxes", "To introduce a single tax on consumption goods and services", "To impose a single tax on wealth and capital gains only", "To reduce taxes on land to encourage agriculture", "To levy a single tax on imports and exports to regulate trade", "To replace all taxes with a single tax on income", "To establish a flat tax rate for all forms of income", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 2, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "economics", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
{"id": "mmlupro-6223", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "Which of the following statements is true of the pupillary light reflex?", "options": ["Its efferent limb is carried in the oculomotor nerve", "Its afferent limb is carried in the trigeminal nerve", "It is mediated by the lateral geniculate body in the thalamus", "Its afferent limb is carried in the oculomotor nerve", "Its efferent limb is carried in the optic nerve", "It is a consensual reflex", "It is mediated by the superior colliculi in the midbrain", "It is mediated by the inferior colliculi in the midbrain", "It is a unilateral reflex", "Its afferent limb is carried in the optic nerve", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 5, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "health", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
