{"id": "mmlupro-384", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "The public always holds the fraction C = (1 / 21) of its M (money supply) in cash and d = (20 / 21) of M in demand deposits, D. The bank is required by law to always have available a reserve ratio, r, of 1/5 of its deposits for withdrawal by bank customers. Verify that if D increases a) the change in the money supply, \\DeltaM, will' be [1 / {(1 / 21) + [(1/5) \u00d7 (20 / 21)]}] = (21 / 5)\\DeltaD, b) the change in demand deposits will be = 4\\DeltaD , and c) the change in cash will be .195 \\DeltaD.", "options": ["(21 / 2) \\DeltaD, 9\\DeltaD, .35\\DeltaD", "(21 / 11) \\DeltaD, 1\\DeltaD, .45\\DeltaD", "(21 / 3) \\DeltaD, 7\\DeltaD, .5\\DeltaD", "(21 / 5) \\DeltaD, 4\\DeltaD, .2\\DeltaD", "(21 / 10) \\DeltaD, 10\\DeltaD, .05\\DeltaD", "(21 / 7) \\DeltaD, 2\\DeltaD, .4\\DeltaD", "(21 / 4) \\DeltaD, 5\\DeltaD, .3\\DeltaD", "(21 / 8) \\DeltaD, 6\\DeltaD, .25\\DeltaD", "(21 / 9) \\DeltaD, 8\\DeltaD, .15\\DeltaD", "(21 / 6) \\DeltaD, 3\\DeltaD, .1\\DeltaD", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 3, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "business", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
