{"id": "mmlupro-1830", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "A homeowner gave his friend a mortgage on his property to secure a loan from the friend to the homeowner in the amount of $100,000. The homeowner then gives an investor a mortgage on the property to secure a loan from the investor to the homeowner in the amount of $80,000. The friend then records his mortgage. The homeowner then gives a bank a mortgage on the property to secure a loan from the bank to the homeowner in the amount of $50,000. The investor then records. The bank then records. The homeowner lost his job and was unable to pay the mortgages on the property. In a foreclosure proceeding in which the friend, the investor, and the bank were parties, the property sold for $160,000. The recording statute in this jurisdiction provided \"unless recorded, all written instruments affecting title to land are void as to subsequent purchasers who paid value and without notice. \"What dollar amount, if any, should go to the friend?", "options": ["$80,000. 00", "$160,000.00", "$100,000. 00", "$20,000.00", "$0. 00", "$50,000.00", "$60,000.00", "$90,000.00", "$30,000. 00", "$70,000.00", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 0, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "law", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "calib"}
{"id": "mmlupro-7622", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "What is the rationale of subtracting expenditures for im-ports in measuring aggregate demand as compared to adding exports as a new component of aggregate demand?", "options": ["Imports are investments in foreign markets, and exports are considered a form of savings", "Imports increase domestic production", "Imports represent domestic consumption, and exports are deducted to avoid double counting in GDP calculations", "Exports are subtracted because they represent an outflow of domestic currency", "Expenditures for imports and exports are both added in measuring aggregate demand", "Exports represent spending on foreign goods", "Imports are not significant to the economy, whereas exports are the main driver of economic growth", "Imports represent spending on foreign goods inducing production abroad, while exports increase domestic production and create jobs.", "Exports represent a transfer of domestic wealth to foreign entities", "Imports and exports are considered equal and cancel each other out in aggregate demand", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 7, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "economics", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
