{"id": "mmlupro-4988", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "This question refers to the following information.\nRead the the following poem to answer questions.\nTake up the White Man's burden\u2014\nSend forth the best ye breed\u2014\nGo bind your sons to exile\nTo serve your captives' need;\nTo wait in heavy harness,\nOn fluttered folk and wild\u2014\nYour new-caught, sullen peoples,\nHalf-devil and half-child.\n...\nTake up the White Man's burden\u2014\nThe savage wars of peace\u2014\nFill full the mouth of Famine\nAnd bid the sickness cease;\nAnd when your goal is nearest\nThe end for others sought\u2026\nWatch sloth and heathen Folly\nBring all your hopes to naught.\nRudyard Kipling, The White Man's Burden, 1899\nBased on this poem, Kipling's conception of the British imperial mission could best be summed up as", "options": ["a glorious, religious responsibility", "a necessary evil for the good of the empire", "a hopeless task with no purpose", "a difficult but necessary task", "a burden that should be willingly undertaken", "a profitable endeavor for the empire", "a mission to educate and enlighten", "a ruthless exercise of power", "a task that is doomed to fail", "an attempt to bring civilization to uncivilized peoples", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 3, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "history", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
{"id": "mmlupro-1713", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "Cooper is suing March for money damages. Because he believes portions of March's deposition are highly favorable to his case, Cooper's attorney intends to read parts of the deposition at trial instead of calling March to the stand. March objects to Cooper's use of the deposition at trial. What is the court's likely ruling?", "options": ["Cooper may use the deposition at trial, but must read the entire deposition, not just selected parts.", "Cooper may use the deposition at trial, but only if he can prove that March's statements are unreliable.", "Cooper may not use the deposition at trial, unless March is unavailable to testify.", "Cooper may not use the deposition at trial, as March is able to testify and no exceptional circumstances exist.", "Cooper may not use the deposition at trial, as this would make March his witness and immune to impeachment.", "Cooper may use the deposition at trial, but only to contradict or impeach March's prior inconsistent statements or pleadings.", "Cooper may use the deposition at trial, but, if requested, he must read all parts that in fairness ought to be considered with the part introduced.", "Cooper may not use the deposition at trial, as it is considered hearsay.", "Cooper may use the deposition at trial, but only if March's attorney is present during the reading.", "Cooper may not use the deposition at trial, as it would violate March's right to confrontation.", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 6, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "law", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
{"id": "mmlupro-2239", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "discuss these two points of view andgive evidence for both sides.", "options": ["Perceptual abilities are determined solely by the immediate physical environment, with no influence from biology or past experiences.", "Human perception is purely innate.", "It is likely that we do have some innate perceptual abilities, and also that they can, to some extent, be modified by experience.", "Perception is a learned skill that has no basis in biology or innate structures.", "The development of perception is a fixed process that remains constant across different environmental conditions.", "Innate perceptual abilities are completely unchangeable and unaffected by learning or experience.", "Perception develops independently of innate abilities and is entirely shaped by cultural influences.", "Perception is the result of a complex interplay between genetic predispositions and sensory experiences.", "Perception only involves individual sensations coming together.", "Perception is solely based on past experiences.", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 2, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "psychology", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "calib"}
