{"id": "mmlupro-5804", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "According to Scott (1990), a document is 'authentic' if it:", "options": ["is a document that includes a detailed account of events", "has been peer-reviewed and approved by a panel of experts", "is representative of all the similar documents that did not survive", "is a document that is free from any alterations or forgeries", "has both a literal and an interpretable meaning", "is a document that has been translated accurately from its original language", "has been verified as authentic by an accredited institution", "is a sincere and accurate account, free from political bias", "is a document that has been officially certified by a notary", "is a 'sound' original, or reliable copy, of known authorship", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 9, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "other", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
{"id": "mmlupro-1592", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "On September 15, a card shop sent the following fax to a printing company: \"Please deliver 100 dozen assorted Christmas cards, delivery by November 1. \"On October 10, the printing company shipped 100 dozen assorted Thanksgiving cards to the card shop, which were received on October 12. The following day, the card shop sent the following fax to the printing company: \"Be advised that your shipment is rejected. Order stipulated Christmas cards, not Thanksgiving cards. \"On October 15, the printing company sent the following fax to the card shop: \"Will ship 100 dozen assorted Christmas cards by November 1. Please ship the Thanksgiving cards back to our warehouse and bill us for the shipping charges. \" This fax was received by the card shop, but the card shop did not respond to it or ship the Thanksgiving cards back to the printing company. On October 25, the printing company attempted to deliver 100 dozen assorted Christmas cards to the card shop, but the latter refused to accept. Did the card shop properly reject the October 25 delivery?", "options": ["No, because the card shop did not return the Thanksgiving cards as requested by the printing company.", "No, because under the UCC a contract for the sale of goods can be modified without consideration.", "Yes, because the printing company did not deliver the correct order initially as requested by the card shop.", "Yes, because the card shop had already rejected the initial shipment of Thanksgiving cards.", "Yes, because the printing company's shipping of the Thanksgiving cards on October 10 constituted a present breach of contract.", "No, because the printing company attempted to rectify the situation by offering to ship the correct cards.", "No, because the card shop did not explicitly agree to the modified offer from the printing company.", "No, because the printing company cured the October 10 defective shipment by its tender of conforming goods on October 25.", "Yes, because the card shop was not obligated to accept the second shipment of Christmas cards.", "Yes, because the printing company's shipping of the Thanksgiving cards on October 10 constituted an anticipatory breach.", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 7, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "law", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
