{"id": "mmlupro-2385", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "Dr. Harry Holliday, a clinical psychologist, is planning to take a three-week cruise. In terms of his clinical practice, Dr. Holliday\u2019s best course of action would be to:", "options": ["give his clients a phone number where he can be reached.", "Arrange for a colleague to provide only emergency sessions, while regular appointments are paused.", "Cancel all appointments for the duration of his vacation without informing his clients.", "hire a colleague to take over his appointments while he is on vacation.", "Continue his sessions via phone calls or video conferencing while on vacation.", "give his clients the phone number of a colleague who has agreed to accept phone calls in emergencies.", "Inform his clients only a day before his departure about his unavailability.", "discuss his vacation plans with his current clients ahead of time so that they know he\u2019ll be unavailable during that time.", "Provide his clients with online resources to manage their issues in his absence.", "Leave without informing his clients of his absence.", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 5, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "psychology", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "calib"}
{"id": "mmlupro-6107", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "During a study of renal glomeruli, a healthy animal kidney is kept in a vascular bath preparation at a constant afferent arterial pressure of 100 mm Hg. If the efferent arteriole is constricted with a vascular clamp, which of the following Starling forces is most likely to change in the glomeruli?", "options": ["Decreased filtration coefficient (Kf)", "No change in Starling forces", "Increased filtration coefficient (Kf)", "Decreased hydrostatic pressure", "Increased hydrostatic pressure", "Increased blood flow", "Increased oncotic pressure", "Decreased oncotic pressure", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 4, "idk_idx": 8, "meta": {"category": "health", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHI", "split": "calib"}
{"id": "mmlupro-1343", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "An off-duty police officer was standing on a street corner waiting for a bus. A man came up from behind and stole the police officer's wallet from his pants pocket. As the man was running away with the wallet, the police officer pulled out his service revolver. The police officer yelled at the man to stop and then fired several shots in the man's direction. The police officer did not aim directly at the man but shot at the pavement intending to frighten him. One of the bullets ricocheted off the sidewalk and struck the man, killing him. The police officer is guilty of", "options": ["reckless endangerment.", "attempted robbery.", "voluntary manslaughter.", "murder.", "aggravated assault.", "no crime, it was self-defense.", "justifiable homicide.", "assault with a deadly weapon.", "negligent homicide.", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 3, "idk_idx": 9, "meta": {"category": "law", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJ", "split": "test"}
{"id": "mmlupro-1610", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "A writer sent a four-page synopsis of an idea for a new television series to a Hollywood producer. He sent it in response to an ad for new ideas in an industry publication. He discussed it with the producer's assistant in a phone call, and mentioned his expectation of compensation. She said, \"Well, of course, we always pay for a writer's work.\" She said she would go over it with her boss to see if he liked it. Several months later, the writer saw a casting call for a new series. The plot and characters were nearly identical to those described in his synopsis. He sued the producer for breach of contract. The producer defended by arguing that there was no contract. What is the likely ruling of the court?", "options": ["The court will rule that there is an express contract because there was a meeting of the mind and mutual assent to the basic terms.", "The court will rule that there can be no contract as the writer didn't explicitly state his expectation for compensation for the idea itself.", "The court will rule that there was no consideration specifically mentioned and under those circumstances, the law viewed the synopsis as a gift to the producer.", "The court will rule that there was an implied in fact contract between the parties based on the conduct that they manifested.", "The court will rule that there was a unilateral contract, with the producer obligated to pay only if he used the idea.", "There were too many terms left out for this to be a contract, and it was too indefinite for the court to imply what the terms might have been.", "The court will rule that the producer's assistant lacked the authority to form a contract, and thus, no contract exists.", "The court will rule that the phone call between the writer and the producer's assistant formed a verbal contract.", "The court will rule that the writer's case is invalid as there was no written agreement.", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 3, "idk_idx": 9, "meta": {"category": "law", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJ", "split": "test"}
{"id": "mmlupro-10299", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "The lunar maria are:", "options": ["dark lavas filling older impact basins", "ancient heavily cratered highlands", "valleys formed by tectonic activity", "lighter colored regions on the Moon", "the Moon's equivalent to Earth's oceans", "the bright regions on the Moon", "dark lavas inside volcanic calderas", "ice-filled craters near the Moon's poles", "high mountain ranges on the Moon", "dark regions caused by meteorite impacts", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 0, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "physics", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
{"id": "mmlupro-11394", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "Find the current that will flow in a series circuit contain-ing a 5-k\\Omega resistor, a 470-\\rhoF capacitor, a 150-mH inductor, and a 0.001\\muF capacitor if the exciting voltage is 65V at 25-kHz.", "options": ["12.5\\angle- 36.3\u00b0mA", "12.0\\angle- 42.0\u00b0 mA", "8.5\\angle- 36.3\u00b0mA", "7.5\\angle- 45.0\u00b0 mA", "10.5\\angle- 36.3\u00b0mA", "10.5\\angle- 30.3\u00b0mA", "13.5\\angle- 30.0\u00b0 mA", "9.5\\angle- 25.0\u00b0 mA", "8.0\\angle- 33.3\u00b0 mA", "11.5\\angle- 40.0\u00b0 mA", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 4, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "engineering", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "calib"}
