{"id": "mmlupro-8007", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "A group of scientists wanted to estimate the proportion of geese returning to the same site for the next breeding season. Suppose they decided to increase the sample size from 200 to 2,000. How will this affect the distribution of the sample proportion?", "options": ["The distribution of the sample proportion will become more uniform.", "The distribution of the sample proportion will be less spread out.", "The shape of the distribution of the sample proportion will change significantly.", "The distribution of the sample proportion will more closely resemble the binomial distribution.", "The distribution of the sample proportion will become skewed.", "The distribution of the sample proportion will be more spread out.", "There will be no noticeable change in the distribution of the sample proportion.", "The spread of the distribution of the sample proportion will remain unaffected.", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 1, "idk_idx": 8, "meta": {"category": "math", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHI", "split": "calib"}
{"id": "mmlupro-1813", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "A woman was the owner of a farm in fee simple. Thewoman left the farm in 1986 to move to the city. Aman took possession of the land in 1987 as an adversepossessor and remained on the land from 1987 to 1997;he then left the property to care for his sick mother forone year, returning the following year, 1999. The man's nephew agreed to live on the farm and take care of it during his uncle's absence. When the man returned from his mother's home in 1999, he continued in possession until 2010 when the womanbrought an ejectment action. Assume that the statutory period for adverse possession in this state is 20 years. The court would most likely hold that", "options": ["the man was entitled to possession, because the woman had abandoned the farm.", "the woman was entitled to possession, because the man's intermittent possession was insufficient to make him an adverse possessor.", "the man was entitled to possession, because his possession was open, notorious, continuous, and hostile as required for the statutory period.", "the woman was entitled to possession, because the man had not paid any property taxes.", "the man's nephew was entitled to possession, as he was the one who took care of the farm during the man's absence.", "the woman was entitled to possession, because the man's absence for a year interrupted the continuity of his possession.", "the woman was the rightful owner and thus entitled to possess the farm.", "the man was entitled to possession, because he had lived on the farm for over 20 years.", "the man was not entitled to possession, as he left the property for a year.", "the man was entitled to possession, because of the privity between the man and his nephew, which aided him in fulfilling the required statutory period.", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 9, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "law", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
{"id": "mmlupro-718", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "Jacob and Sons Plumbing bought a forklift for $10,000. The forklift is expected to last 5 years, and to have a residual value of $3,000. Jacob wishes to use the straight line depreciation method, while his sons wish to use the sum-of-the-years'-digits method. What will the difference in the depreciation allowances be for the third year?", "options": ["$150", "$400", "$300", "$500", "$600", "$250", "$100", "$350", "$200", "zero", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 9, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "business", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
{"id": "mmlupro-10169", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "The equation E = mc^2 indicates that energy", "options": ["is equal to the square of the speed of light.", "equals mass divided by the speed of light squared.", "equals mass multiplied by the speed of light.", "is inversely proportional to mass.", "and mass are not related at all.", "equals the sum of mass and the speed of light squared.", "equals mass moving at the speed of light squared.", "and mass are closely related.", "equals moving mass.", "is fundamentally different than mass.", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 7, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "physics", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
{"id": "mmlupro-591", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "ABC Plumbing has the following current assets and liabilities: Cash, $7,300; Marketable Securities, $14,200, Accounts Receivable, $2,120; Notes Payable, $1,400; Accounts Payable, $1,850. Find the acid-test ratio for ABC, correct to the nearest hundredth.", "options": ["9.27", "8.27", "5.27", "8.77", "7.27", "7.77", "6.77", "7.17", "6.27", "4.27", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 4, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "business", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
{"id": "mmlupro-3238", "pool": "mmlu_pro", "domain": "general", "question": "What is meant by a gene pool, balanced polymorphism, and genetic load?", "options": ["Gene pool is the total number of alleles in a population; balanced polymorphism is the maintenance of two or more alleles at a locus by natural selection; genetic load is the proportion of individuals in a population with genetic defects.", "Gene pool is the collection of genes in a single organism; balanced polymorphism is the variation of a single gene; genetic load is the number of genes in an organism.", "Gene pool is the total number of organisms in a population; balanced polymorphism is a genetic imbalance; genetic load is the genetic weight of an organism.", "Gene pool refers to a single gene; balanced polymorphism refers to a dominance of one gene; genetic load refers to the genetic burden of an organism.", "Gene pool refers to the physical pool where genes are stored; balanced polymorphism is the imbalance of allele frequencies; genetic load is the amount of genetic information carried by an organism.", "Gene pool is the set of all genetic traits in a biological community; balanced polymorphism is when one allele is favored over others; genetic load is the genetic contribution of an organism to its offspring.", "Gene pool is the sum of all genetic variations in a closed environment; balanced polymorphism is the equal representation of all alleles in a population; genetic load is the accumulated genetic mutations in a population.", "Gene pool is the sum total of genes in a population; balanced polymorphism is when different forms of a genotype are maintained in equilibrium over time; genetic load is the reduction in average fitness due to presence of suboptimal forms.", "Gene pool is the diversity of genes in a population; balanced polymorphism is the dominance of a single gene; genetic load is the genetic capacity of an organism.", "Gene pool is the total genetic information in the gametes of a population; balanced polymorphism is the consistent occurrence of a single allele; genetic load is the genetic diversity within a species.", "I cannot answer this question with confidence."], "gold_idx": 7, "idk_idx": 10, "meta": {"category": "biology", "source": "MMLU-Pro"}, "letters": "ABCDEFGHIJK", "split": "test"}
